ice company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are the Authorized Parts and Service Distributor for more than 50 manufacturers and can get all the parts you need.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='casco-food-equipment-services-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cass County Electric Cooperative is headquartered in Fargo, North Dakota, and has operated as a member-owned electric cooperative since 1937.

The cooperative distributes electricity across a service territory that spans 10 counties, maintaining nearly 6,000 miles of distribution line and 41 substations. It provides power to nearly 61,000 members, including residential, commercial, agricultural, and apartment accounts. Beyond delivery, the cooperative offers member services such as outage monitoring, bill payment, service start/stop/transfer, energy conservation programs, and safety education.

Its customer base includes residential urban and farm accounts, commercial businesses, irrigation operations, and lighting services. The cooperative also supports the broader community through programs like Operation Round Up, which funds local organizations, scholarships and youth programs, and partnerships with community events across its service area.

The cooperative distinguishes itself through its not-for-profit, member-governed structure. A locally elected board of directors sets policy, and the organization emphasizes safety, integrity, innovation, accountability, and community investment as core values. Profits are returned to members as capital credits, and decisions are made with long-term community benefit in mind.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electric distribution", "Outage monitoring and reporting", "Service start/stop/transfer", "Energy conservation and management programs", "Electrical safety education", "Capital credits allocation", "Community grant program (Operation Round Up)", "Scholarships and youth programs", "Community partnerships and event support"], "industries": ["Electric utility", "Energy management", "Community development", "Agricultural services", "Residential services", "Commercial services"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Electric distribution lines", "Substations"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Member-owned, not-for-profit cooperative structure", "Locally governed by an elected board of member-directors", "6,000 miles of distribution line and 41 substations", "Community reinvestment through Operation Round Up and scholarships", "Safety-first culture embedded in operations and public education"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1937 -> /about-us", "Member-owned electric cooperative -> /about-us", "Serves nearly 61,000 members across 10 counties -> /about-us", "Maintains nearly 6,000 miles of distribution line and 41 substations -> /about-us", "Headquarters Fargo, ND -> db, /about-us", "Service centers in Fargo, Kindred, Arthur, Lisbon, Valley City -> /about-us", "Service counties: Cass, Barnes, Traill, Richland, Ransom, Sargent, Dickey, LaMoure, Steele, Stutsman -> /about-us", "Mission and values (Safety, Integrity, Innovation, Accountability, Community) -> /about-us", "Community programs: Operation Round Up, Scholarships & Youth Programs, Community Partnerships -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Cass County Electric Cooperative is a member-owned electric cooperative serving nearly 61,000 members across 10 counties in southeastern North Dakota.", "founded_year": "1937", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/cass-county-electric-cooperative/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cass-county-electric-cooperative' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Castellano Custom Furniture operates from a workshop and showroom on North Columbia Boulevard in Portland, Oregon. The company was founded more than 40 years ago as a family venture and remains three generations strong, though the exact founding year and founders'' names are not publicly disclosed.

The firm manufactures custom upholstered furniture—sofas, sectionals, loveseats, chairs, and ottomans—entirely in its Portland facility. It offers a full design-to-build service: consultation, collaborative design, and handcrafted production using locally sourced alder frames, domestically produced foam, recycled steel springs, and eco-friendly textiles. The operation also maintains a curated pre-made collection. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

The company sells directly to homeowners and also works with design professionals on custom projects. No specific commercial or institutional clients are named.

Castellano emphasizes sustainability and durability as differentiators: waste-free manufacturing that recycles sawdust into heating fuel and foam scraps into carpet padding, lifetime warranties on frames and springs, and a commitment to biodegradable or recyclable materials. The business was started on the belief that every piece should be as unique as the person designing it.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted furniture manufacturing", "Upholstery", "Woodworking (alder frames)", "Foam fabrication", "Spring assembly (recycled steel)", "Finishing", "Sustainable manufacturing (waste recycling)", "Design consultation", "Trade/designer portal"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Interior design", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Alder wood", "Foam (locally made)", "Recycled steel springs", "Recycled polyester fibers", "Environmentally approved dyes", "Biodegradable/recyclable materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime warranties on frames and springs", "Waste-free manufacturing (sawdust to heating fuel, foam scraps to carpet padding)", "Locally made in Portland using responsibly grown alder and local foam", "Eco-friendly textiles from recycled polyester and approved dyes", "Custom design collaboration from concept to completion"], "facts_used": ["Location: Portland, OR -> /", "Family-owned, three generations -> /", "Custom furniture manufacturing in Portland -> /", "Lifetime warranties on frames and springs -> /", "Sustainable practices: waste-free, recycled materials -> /", "Designer portal for trade -> /", "Materials: alder, foam, recycled steel, recycled polyester -> /", "Showroom address: 220 N. Columbia Blvd, Portland, OR 97217 -> /", "No explicit founding year stated -> /", "No employee count stated -> /", "No certifications mentioned -> /", "No equipment named -> /", "No volume, lead time, tolerances stated -> /", "No export compliance, languages, social links in input -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our handcrafted furniture is produced entirely in Portland, reducing carbon emissions and energy consumption.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='castellano-custom-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Catalyst Communications was founded in 1997 in Forest, Virginia, a community in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains near Lynchburg. The company emerged as a provider of Radio Control over IP solutions for critical communications agencies.

The firm develops its own dispatch console system, Propulsion™, a transportable communications tool called ICE™, and an interoperability platform named IntelliLink that bridges land mobile radio and LTE networks. Its engineering focus spans software development, IP network optimization, and standards-based interfaces for P25, DMR, and mission-critical push-to-talk over cellular. With over 25 years in the market, Catalyst supports agencies nationwide from its Virginia headquarters.

Customers include public safety, utility, education, transportation, and government organizations. Concrete references cite the Florida Highway Patrol, Federal Land Management Agencies, Honolulu public safety agencies, the Dallas Georgia Police Department, a county public safety district, an electric cooperative, and a state forestry commission. The company also partners with FirstNet and Southern Linc to extend its interoperability reach.

Catalyst says its differentiation rests on being first to market with Radio Control over IP technology, holding licenses with numerous radio manufacturers for advanced digital control, and developing the P25 CSSI/DFSI, DMR AIS, and 3GPP MCPTT interfaces. It also emphasizes 24/7 customer support as a core commitment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Radio Control over IP solutions", "Dispatch console systems (Propulsion\u2122)", "Transportable communications (ICE\u2122)", "Interoperability and interworking solutions (IntelliLink)", "Software development for land mobile radio", "IP network engineering and bandwidth management", "Standards development (P25 CSSI/DFSI, DMR AIS, 3GPP MCPTT)", "24/7 customer support"], "industries": ["Public Safety", "Utilities", "Education", "Transportation", "Government", "Federal Land Management", "Electric Cooperatives", "Forestry"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Propulsion\u2122 dispatch console", "ICE\u2122 transportable communications tool", "IntelliLink interoperability platform"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First to market with Radio Control over IP technology", "Licenses and agreements with many radio manufacturers for advanced digital control", "Developed P25 CSSI/DFSI, DMR AIS, and 3GPP MCPTT standard interfaces", "Over 25 years supporting public safety, utility, government, and education markets", "24/7 customer support"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1997 -> /about", "Headquartered in Forest, VA -> /", "Products: Propulsion\u2122, ICE\u2122, IntelliLink -> /", "Industries served: Public Safety, Utility, Education, Transportation, Government -> /", "Partnerships with Florida Highway Patrol, Federal Land Management Agencies, Honolulu public safety agencies, Dallas Georgia Police Department, county public safety district, electric cooperative, state forestry commission -> /", "First to market with Radio Control over IP technology -> /", "Over 25 years experience -> /", "Standards support: P25 CSSI/DFSI, DMR AIS, 3GPP MCPTT -> /", "24/7 customer support -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Catalyst is a market leader in providing Radio Control over IP solutions to Critical Communications agencies.", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/catalyst-communications-technologies/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='catalyst-communications' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cay Electronics is based in Portsmouth, Rhode Island, and has been providing marine systems engineering services for over 40 years. The company serves clients throughout New England and worldwide, including boat owners, builders, shipyards, captains, and crew.

The firm offers a full range of marine electronics and electrical services: system design, equipment sales and wholesale distribution, installation, commissioning, consulting, and repair. As authorized dealers for marine manufacturers, they supply navigation, communication, audio/video, networking, and electrical power systems. Certified technicians follow in-house installation standards, and the company maintains a large inventory for same-day shipping worldwide.

Cay Electronics works with recreational and commercial marine customers, from trailer boats to superyachts and workboat fleets. Their projects cover navigation and charting, autopilot, radar, sonar, satellite communications (including Starlink and Iridium), battery systems (gel, AGM, lithium), electric propulsion, solar installations, digital switching, and CCTV.

