shipping and same-day shipping from large inventory -> /", "Dealers for top marine manufacturers -> /", "Consulting, system design, equipment supply, installation, commissioning, service & repairs -> /services", "Customer types: boat owners, builders, yards, captains, crew -> /", "Commercial marine electronics, workboats, fleets -> /services", "Specific electronics categories: navigation, autopilot, radar, sonar, satellite comms, battery systems, electric propulsion, solar, digital switching, CCTV -> /services", "Detailed system drawings with auto-generated BOMs and wire lists -> /", "Commissioning includes firmware updates, sea trials, hands-on instruction -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Cay Electronics sets the standard in marine & mobile systems engineering. Delivering efficient, reliable solutions in design, sales, installation, repairs, and more.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cay-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Central Electric Cooperative is a member-owned, not-for-profit electric utility headquartered in Mitchell, South Dakota. While its exact founding year is not publicly stated in available materials, the cooperative has long served rural communities in the region with electricity and related energy services.

The cooperative provides electric distribution across its service territory and operates a member-facing platform called SmartHub for energy usage monitoring, bill payment, and service requests. Beyond power delivery, it runs a full-service department offering appliance sales and repair, heating and cooling installation and maintenance (including heat pumps and mini-splits), and electrical wiring for both agricultural and residential customers. Additional offerings include generator sales, solar well pump installation, and a distributed energy application process for members pursuing renewable generation. A dedicated Betts Road Service Center supports these hands-on services.

Concrete examples from its programs include rebates for energy-efficient heat pumps and water heaters, youth scholarships and leadership tours, and the Operation Round-Up program that rounds up member bills to fund community grants. The cooperative also assists members with distributed energy interconnection and load management.

The cooperative model itself is the primary differentiator: as a not-for-profit, margins are returned to members as capital credits. The organization emphasizes local governance, community reinvestment through grants and safety education, and a service-first approach summarized in its messaging about why cooperatives still matter.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electric service connection and transfer", "Outage reporting and mapping", "Appliance sales and service", "Heating and cooling installation and service (HVAC, heat pumps, mini-splits)", "Electrical wiring (agricultural and residential)", "Generator sales and service", "Solar well pump installation", "Distributed energy application processing", "Load management", "Energy efficiency rebates", "Capital credits allocation", "Youth programs and scholarships", "Operation Round-Up community funding", "Safety education (power line, grain bin, generator)"], "industries": ["Residential electric service", "Agricultural electric service", "Commercial electric service", "Renewable energy integration", "Energy efficiency programs"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Not-for-profit cooperative returning capital credits to members", "Member rebates on energy-efficient equipment", "Community grant programs and youth scholarships", "SmartHub energy monitoring and payment platform", "Local service department for wiring, HVAC, and appliance needs"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Mitchell, South Dakota -> db", "Member-owned not-for-profit cooperative structure -> /", "Services: electric distribution, appliance sales/service, HVAC, electrical wiring -> /", "SmartHub energy monitoring platform -> /", "Rebates on heat pumps and water heaters -> /", "Capital credits returned to members -> /", "Community programs: Operation Round-Up, youth scholarships, grants -> /", "Distributed energy and solar application process -> /", "Betts Road Servi