ration, Novelis Aluminum, BGCAPP -> /", "Mission: listen to needs, develop custom products within timeline, quality workmanship within economical means, never sacrifice safety/quality/integrity, exceptional customer service, employee resources/education, respect employees -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Central Kentucky Industrial consists of a full service fabrication shop outfitted with metal fabrication equipment where we construct our duct work and system components", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='central-kentucky-industrial-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Central Wire Industries operates from Perris, California, and traces its roots to 1955 when it began producing fine-diameter red-metal wire for fourdrinier fabric used in paper manufacturing. The company later expanded into stainless-steel fine wire and grew through acquisitions across the United States, Canada, and the United Kingdom. As of August 2026, the Central Wire Group of Companies is owned by Altair Industries, a private-equity firm focused on aerospace, defense, and mission-critical industrial businesses.

The company manufactures a broad line of specialty wire products including bar stock, cold-heading wire, fine and ultra-fine wire, knitted wire mesh, resistance wire, shaped and profiled wire, slicklines, spring wire, and welding wire. Processes cover rod processing, breakdown drawing, centerless grinding, custom profiling, knitting, and both destructive and non-destructive testing. With 11 locations in three countries and more than 750 employees, Central Wire serves both mission-critical and commercial markets.

Customers span aerospace, architecture, automotive, medical, military and defense, oil and gas, and food and beverage industries. Products are used in mission-critical fastening systems, heating coils for appliances and flooring, downhole slicklines for sour and sweet environments, and welding consumables for MIG, TIG, and submerged-arc processes.

