UPDATE companies SET description='City Food Equipment operates a 45,000-square-foot store and showroom in Lombard, Illinois, a village in DuPage County about 22 miles west of Chicago. The facility is open to the public six days a week, offering wholesale pricing to both food-service professionals and home cooks.

The company stocks new and used commercial restaurant equipment from brands such as Hobart, Vulcan, True Manufacturing, and Manitowoc, with up to 1,000 pieces on display at any time. An in-house team of technicians inspects, repairs, and refurbishes each used unit before it reaches the sales floor, a process the company says covers meat-processing, deli, and bakery machinery. The showroom also carries thousands of smallwares and supplies for front- and back-of-house needs.

Customers include restaurants, bars, bakeries, delis, catering operations, and meat-processing facilities, as well as individual home chefs. The product range spans cooking equipment (ranges, fryers, ovens, griddles, charbroilers), refrigeration, meat-processing tools (grinders, slicers, saws, mixers, stuffers), and bakery mixers and dividers.

City Food Equipment describes itself as one of the nation''s largest used-restaurant-equipment dealers and highlights its certified technicians who refurbish Hobart planetary mixers to original manufacturer specifications. The company emphasizes its rigorous restoration process and the breadth of inventory available for immediate purchase.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["New commercial restaurant equipment sales", "Used equipment refurbishment", "In-house equipment inspection and repair", "Commercial kitchen supply distribution", "Meat processing equipment sales", "Bakery equipment sales", "Deli equipment sales"], "industries": ["Restaurant", "Bar", "Bakery", "Deli", "Meat processing", "Catering", "Food service", "Home cooking"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the nation''s largest used restaurant equipment dealers", "In-house technicians inspect, repair, and refurbish every used unit", "Certified technicians restore Hobart mixers to manufacturer specifications", "45,000 sq. ft. showroom with up to 1,000 pieces on display", "Wholesale pricing open to the public"], "facts_used": ["Location: Lombard, IL, DuPage County, 22 miles west of Chicago -> /", "Store size: 45,000 sq. ft. -> /", "Up to 1,000 pieces of new and used equipment on display -> /", "Brands carried: Hobart, Biro, Berkel, Bizerba, Vulcan, Compass, Continental, True Mfg., Imperial, Manitowoc, Scotsman -> /", "In-house technicians inspect, analyze, repair/refurbish used equipment -> /", "Specializes in used meat processing, deli, and bakery equipment -> /", "Certified technicians refurbish Hobart commercial dough mixers to manufacturer specs -> /", "Open to public at wholesale prices -> /", "Store hours: Mon-Fri 8-5:30, Sat 9-1, closed Sun -> /", "Industries served: restaurants, bars, bakeries, delis, catering, meat processing, home chefs -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "City Food Equipment''s restaurant supply store located in Lombard... provides local restauranteurs and other food service establishment owners and operators a convenient place to shop for restaurant equipment and commercial kitchen supplies.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='city-food-equipment-lombard-il-new-used-restaurant-equipment-kitchen-supply-store' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='City Hardwoods operates from Birmingham, Alabama, where it runs a sawmill, kiln-drying facility, and showroom The business was acquired in June 2022 by Caleb Gilbert, who runs the family-owned small business with his father. Gilbert’s path to woodworking began during his senior year at LSU when a shoulder injury sidelined him from baseball; he filled the time with weekend shop projects and soon shared the passion with his father, a lifelong hobbyist. Together they started milling and drying hardwood lumber for their own custom furniture projects.

The company’s remote sawmill salvages hundreds of urban logs each year from local tree services, diverting material that would otherwise become mulch. Logs are milled, stacked, and air-dried before finishing in one of two kilns—a dehumidification kiln and a vacuum kiln—that produce sterilized, kiln-dried lumber. Every board and slab is then surfaced on a planer or flattened on a slab CNC, a step that lets customers see grain, character, and color in the showroom. City Hardwoods builds custom furniture and retails the kiln-dried hardwood lumber, but does not offer milling or drying services to the public.

The primary customers are woodworkers, furniture buyers, and the broader Birmingham community seeking local hardwoods. The shop supplies lumber for custom furniture projects and sells boards directly to hobbyists and professionals through its retail showroom.

Gilbert says the operation was born from a desire to cut out middlemen and give each log a unique story. The dual-kiln setup ensures lumber is free of pests, and the slab CNC provides a showroom-ready surface that differentiates the buying experience. The acquisition of the existing City Hardwoods retailer in 2022 gave the family a platform to scale their sawmill output into a combined manufacturing and retail operation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture making", "Sawmilling (urban log salvage)", "Air drying", "Kiln drying (dehumidification and vacuum)", "Planing", "Slab CNC flattening", "Hardwood lumber retail"], "industries": ["Custom furniture", "Hardwood lumber retail", "Urban lumber"], "materials": ["Hardwood", "Urban logs"], "equipment": ["Dehumidification kiln", "Vacuum kiln", "Planer", "Slab CNC", "Sawmill"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Remote sawmill operation salvaging urban logs destined for mulch", "Two kilns (dehumidification and vacuum) producing sterilized kiln-dried lumber", "Slab CNC surfacing for showroom-ready boards", "Family-owned small business", "Acquired existing hardwood retailer in June 2022"], "facts_used": ["Location: Birmingham, Alabama -> /", "Address: 138 West Valley Ave, Birmingham, AL 35209 -> /", "Acquired in June 2022 -> /about", "Owner: Caleb Gilbert -> /about", "Family-owned small business -> /about, /", "Remote sawmill operation salvaging urban logs -> /, /about", "Two kilns: dehumidification and vacuum -> /, /about", "Slab CNC for surfacing -> /, /about", "Custom furniture making and lumber retail -> /, /about", "No public milling/drying services -> /about", "Instagram handle @cityhardwoods -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Furniture Makers. Sawmill / Kiln Operators. Hardwood Lumber Retailers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [],