UPDATE companies SET description='Cold River Furniture operates from South Acworth, New Hampshire, where master furniture maker Peter Maynard established his workshop in 1975 after completing an apprenticeship at the George Whitmore Furniture Company in Middletown, Connecticut. Maynard, who began his training at age 18 under second- and third-generation Connecticut River Valley craftsmen, moved to the upper Connecticut River Valley to start his own company. His wife, Marcie, has been integral to the business since its inception, handling communications and project coordination.

The studio produces original, handcrafted fine furniture using select North American hardwoods. Maynard combines antique water-powered machinery — including a 19th-century tenoning machine — with modern tools and extensive handwork. Joinery relies on full mortise-and-tenon and hand-cut dovetails, supplemented by Chinese and Japanese woodworking techniques. Each piece undergoes multiple sanding rounds, three coats of stain, and six coats of thin tung oil varnish. The workshop also handles log procurement, sawing flitch-matched lumber, and careful drying. Output is limited to signed, one-of-a-kind pieces shipped across North America.

Clients include private collectors, interior designers, and institutions such as the Metropolitan Museum of Art, which has commissioned work.

Maynard emphasizes a connection to the New England landscape and a commitment to integrity in craft. He describes the work as a deliberate alternative to mass production, where the mark of the human hand is central. The company''s philosophy centers on creating heirloom pieces that gain value over time, rooted in a lifestyle of simplicity and focus.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted furniture making", "Mortise and tenon joinery", "Hand-cut dovetail joinery", "Japanese woodworking techniques", "Chinese woodworking techniques", "Wood selection and milling (flitch-matched)", "Log procurement and sawing", "Lumber drying", "Hand finishing (stain, tung oil varnish)"], "industries": ["Fine furniture", "High-end residential", "Museum and collector commissions", "Interior design"], "materials": ["North American hardwoods", "Select hardwoods", "Prime logs", "Flitch-matched lumber"], "equipment": ["19th-century water-powered tenoning machine", "Antique mill machines", "Modern woodworking machinery", "Hand tools"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Signed original heirloom pieces that accrue value over time", "Hand-selected, flitch-matched lumber sourced from local forests", "Blend of 19th-century water-powered machinery and traditional hand tools", "Incorporation of Chinese and Japanese woodworking methods", "Multi-step hand-finishing with three coats stain and six coats tung oil varnish"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 in South Acworth, NH -> /about", "Peter Maynard apprenticed at George Whitmore Furniture Company 1974 -> /about", "Marcie Maynard involved from beginning 1975 -> /about", "Handcrafted furniture using antique water-powered machinery and hand tools -> /about", "Mortise and tenon, hand-cut dovetails, Japanese/Chinese methods -> /about", "Finishing: three coats stain, six coats tung oil varnish -> /about", "Signed original heirloom pieces -> /about", "Commissioned by Metropolitan Museum of Art -> /about", "Featured in NY Times, Boston Globe, Architectural Digest -> /about", "Awards: Best in Living with Craft 2018, Best Wood Furniture 2019, 2020 -> /", "Ships across North America -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Peter Maynard, Master Furniture Maker... makes original furniture that ships all over North America.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cold-river-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Billerica, Massachusetts, ColdSnap designs and sells a commercial frozen treat machine and a line of shelf‑stable pods that produce frozen desserts and beverages on demand.

The ColdSnap machine accepts pre‑filled pods containing a liquid base that is churned and frozen in roughly two to three minutes, delivering ice cream, frozen lattes, protein shakes, smoothies, or non‑dairy treats without the need for refrigeration or cleaning. The pods remain shelf‑stable for up to nine months, simplifying inventory compared with conventional frozen products. ColdSnap also provides diagnostics and repair services for its equipment.

