CMNE highlights four core differentiators: end-to-end support with manufacturing, packaging, storage, and shipping under one roof; scalable solutions built for any brand stage; a quality-driven commitment to consistency, safety, and regulatory compliance; and a brand-focused philosophy that ties the company''s success directly to its clients'' growth.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Research & Development (R&D)", "Co-Manufacturing", "Co-Packing", "Private Labeling", "Ingredient Sourcing", "Food Manufacturing", "Storage", "Fulfillment", "Shipping", "Logistics Coordination"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end manufacturing, packaging, storage, and shipping under one roof", "Scalable solutions built to support startups through established brands", "Quality-driven consistency, safety, and compliance", "Brand-focused approach aligning company success with client growth"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bristol, Connecticut -> db", "Full-service food manufacturing facility -> /", "Services: R&D, co-manufacturing, co-packing, private labeling, storage, fulfillment, shipping -> /", "Customers: food brands from startups to established brands -> /", "Differentiators: end-to-end support, scalable solutions, quality-driven, brand-focused -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Manufacturing NE (CMNE) is a full-service food manufacturing facility built to help brands grow\u2014from concept to consumer.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='contract-manufacturing-ne' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Contract Medical Manufacturing (CMM) operates from Oxford, Connecticut, just off Interstate 84 between Boston and New York City. The company was formed in 2007 as a spin-off of Doctors Research Group, Inc., with roots tracing back to 2000. Richard Deslauriers, a mechanical engineer and physician who previously worked at Johnson & Johnson and Medtronic, established CMM to provide full-service contract manufacturing for the medical device market.

CMM specializes in mechanical and electromechanical assembly of Class I and Class II sterile and non-sterile medical devices. Its capabilities extend beyond assembly to include supply chain management, supplier qualification, inventory control, process development and validation, statistical analysis, device testing, packaging, labeling, and coordination of third-party sterilization. The facility houses precision machining equipment such as an Okuma MX45VAE vertical machining center (30×19×17.5 in, 20-tool magazine) and an Okuma CNC lathe with a 12-tool turret, enabling in-house component production. The company operates under FDA 21 CFR Part 820 and ISO 13485:2016 quality systems.

CMM serves medical device companies ranging from Fortune 100 corporations to early-stage startups, positioning itself as a co-development partner rather than a pure outsourcing vendor. Customers rely on CMM for single-source management of purchasing, incoming inspection, warehousing, assembly, testing, packaging, and distribution.

