UPDATE companies SET description='CoolCAD Electronics operates from Greenbelt, Maryland, where it designs and fabricates semiconductor devices and chips from wide-bandgap silicon carbide (SiC). The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm produces SiC MOSFETs, diodes, high-temperature integrated circuits, and deep-ultraviolet optical sensors. Its proprietary SiC formulations and manufacturing processes enable devices that operate continuously at temperatures exceeding 400 °C, well above the 200 °C limit of conventional silicon chips. CoolCAD also offers research and development services, computer-aided design and thermal simulation through its CoolSPICE software, cryogenic and radiation testing for space and nuclear applications, and engineering support for transitioning existing silicon-based power devices to SiC.

Customers span aerospace, automotive, data communications, green energy, military and defense, power generation, and water purification sectors. The company''s high-temperature ICs and UV sensors are positioned for extreme-environment applications such as deep-space exploration, nuclear energy monitoring, and daylight UV imaging without optical filters.

CoolCAD holds multiple U.S. patents covering wide-bandgap SiC semiconductor advances. The technology was developed to accelerate the shift from fossil-fuel infrastructure toward renewable energy systems by delivering higher voltage, higher power, and smaller, lighter electronic systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SiC semiconductor device design", "SiC semiconductor fabrication", "SiC MOSFET manufacturing", "SiC diode manufacturing", "High-temperature IC fabrication", "Deep UV optical sensor fabrication", "Research and development", "Computer-aided design and simulation (CoolSPICE)", "Cryogenic testing", "Radiation testing", "SiC technology transition services"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Automotive", "Data Communications", "Green Energy", "Military & Defense", "Power Generation", "Water Purification"], "materials": ["Silicon Carbide (SiC)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SiC devices operate at temperatures up to and beyond 400 \u00b0C", "Proprietary SiC formulations and manufacturing processes", "Deep UV optical sensors function in broad daylight without special filters", "Multiple U.S. patents in wide-bandgap SiC semiconductors", "CoolSPICE software for IC design and thermal simulation"], "facts_used": ["Designs and fabricates SiC semiconductor devices and chips -> /", "Headquartered in Greenbelt, Maryland -> db", "SiC devices operate at temperatures up to and beyond 400\u00b0C -> /", "Proprietary SiC formulations and manufacturing processes -> /", "Flagship products: SiC MOSFETs, Diodes, High-Temp ICs, UV Optical Sensors -> /", "Core competencies: R&D (multiple US patents), CoolSPICE software, Cryogenic & Radiation Testing, SiC transition services -> /", "Industries served: Aerospace, Automotive, Data Communications, Green Energy, Military & Defense, Power Generation, Water Purification -> /", "Authors of e-book: Neil Goldsman and Christopher Darmody -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CoolCAD Electronics is an innovative company that designs and fabricates semiconductor devices and chips made from wide bandgap semiconductor Silicon Carbide (SiC).", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='coolcad-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cooper Lighting Solutions, a business unit of Signify, is headquartered in Peachtree City, Georgia.

The company manufactures LED lighting fixtures and controls across a portfolio of brands including HALO, PrentaLux, WaveLinx, Nemalux, Metalux, and Lumark. Its Americus, Georgia facility has earned NEMA Make It American certification, verifying domestic content compliance. The product range spans commercial downlights, high-bay luminaires, outdoor lighting, marine-grade fixtures, decorative luminaires, and wireless control systems such as WaveLinx with DMX integration. Manufacturing capabilities include pressure-equalization valve technology, 3D-printed decorative shades, and design-for-disassembly practices that avoid glue, paint, or potting.

Cooper Lighting Solutions serves commercial, industrial, marine, hospitality, multi-family, retail, and manufacturing sectors. Its products are specified by architects, engineers, and contractors for applications ranging from office and retail spaces to harsh marine environments and large-scale industrial facilities. The company also provides building-readiness tools for life-safety and egress lighting testing.

The company emphasizes sustainability and transparency: all PrentaLux products carry Declare labels disclosing material content above 100 ppm, and the firm targets net-zero emissions by 2040 through its parent Signify. Its "Closing the Loop" initiative enables product refreshment without full replacement, and the NEMA Make It American certification underscores a commitment to domestic manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 1598A','NEMA Make It American Certified','Declare-certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["LED lighting fixture manufacturing", "Lighting controls manufacturing", "Product design and engineering", "UL 1598A certified marine-grade manufacturing", "Pressure equalization technology", "3D printing for decorative accessories", "Wireless lighting controls (WaveLinx)", "Emergency lighting systems", "Outdoor lighting manufacturing", "High bay lighting manufacturing", "Downlight manufacturing", "Decorative lighting manufacturing", "Design for disassembly", "Building readiness tools"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Marine", "Hospitality", "Multi-family", "Retail", "Manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NEMA Make It American Certified facility in Americus, Georgia", "Declare-certified PrentaLux products with full material transparency", "Pressure-equalization valve technology for fixture longevity", "3D-printed decorative shades for customizable aesthetics", "WaveLinx wireless controls with DMX integration and acoustic sensing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1833 -> db", "Headquartered in Peachtree City, Georgia -> db", "Business unit of Signify -> /about-us", "Manufactures LED lighting fixtures and controls -> db", "Brands: HALO, PrentaLux, WaveLinx, Nemalux, Metalux, Lumark -> /", "Americus, Georgia facility NEMA Make It American Certified -> /", "UL 1598A marine certification -> /", "Pressure equalization valve technology -> /", "3D printed decorative shades