UPDATE companies SET description='CorVent Medical, Inc. is based in Fargo, North Dakota, where it designs and manufactures critical care respiratory ventilation solutions. The company’s flagship product, the RESPOND® Ventilator, is developed and built in the United States to serve hospitals, long-term care facilities, government stockpiles, and rural health clinics. CorVent Medical emphasizes simplicity, safety, and smart technology to reduce complexity in critical care ventilation.

The RESPOND® Ventilator provides ICU-standard ventilation in a lightweight, portable platform. It supports invasive and non-invasive modes for patients from pediatrics (≥38 kg) through adults, with adjustable settings for flow triggering, oxygen concentration, and PEEP. Built-in safeguards include high inspiratory pressure, disconnect, and apnea alarms. The system operates with any low-flow oxygen source, uses multi-stage antiviral filters rated at 99.99% efficiency, and requires no proprietary circuits or high-pressure gas. A hot-swappable battery provides up to three hours of runtime, while nurse call ports and EMR connectivity enable remote monitoring and documentation. CorVent Medical backs the device with a five-year standard warranty and eliminates service and maintenance contracts.

The company serves acute care hospitals, critical access hospitals (CACs), long-term care hospitals (LTCHs), skilled nursing facilities (SNFs), and government stockpile managers. Its customer base includes respiratory therapy directors, chief nursing officers, ICU directors, and financial officers. CorVent Medical offers nationwide product demonstrations and evaluations to support procurement decisions.

The company holds ISO 13485 certification and complies with FDA 21 CFR 820.30 and current Good Manufacturing Practices (cGMP). Its differentiators include a five-year warranty without service contracts, no proprietary consumables, and independence from high-pressure oxygen infrastructure.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','21 CFR 820.30','cGMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Critical care ventilator design and manufacturing", "Invasive and non-invasive ventilation modes", "Remote patient monitoring and EMR integration", "Antiviral filtration (99.99% efficiency)", "Low-flow oxygen source compatibility", "Product demonstration and evaluation services"], "industries": ["Hospitals", "Critical access hospitals", "Long-term care hospitals", "Skilled nursing facilities", "Government stockpiles", "Rural health clinics", "Private care providers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["5-year standard warranty with no service contracts", "No proprietary circuits or filters required", "No high-pressure oxygen infrastructure needed", "Designed and manufactured in the USA", "ISO 13485 certified and FDA cGMP compliant"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fargo, North Dakota -> db", "ISO 13485 certified -> /about-us", "Compliant with 21 CFR 820.30 -> /about-us", "Compliant with cGMP -> /about-us", "RESPOND\u00ae Ventilator product -> /", "5-year standard warranty -> /", "No service or maintenance contracts -> /", "No proprietary circuits or BV filters -> /", "No high-pressure oxygen gas sources required -> /", "Designed and built in the USA -> /", "Invasive and non-invasive ventilation modes -> /", "Pediatric (\u226538 kg) to adult patients -> /", "Hot-swappable battery up to 3 hours -> /", "Nurse call port and EMR connectivity -> /", "Multi-stage antiviral filters 99.99% efficiency -> /", "Works with all low-flow O2 sources -> /", "Serves hospitals, LTCHs, SNFs, government stockpiles -> /", "Nationwide demos and evaluations -> /", "Mission to reduce complexity through Simple, Safe, Smart technologies -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The RESPOND\u00ae Ventilator was developed to address the urgent need for reliable, efficient, and safe medical ventilation systems.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='corvent-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corbeau was founded in 1966 in Bluffdale, Utah, and has spent more than six decades developing high-performance seating. The company operates from a facility in the Salt Lake City area, where it designs and manufactures seats for street, race, off-road, gaming, and office applications.

The product line includes reclining and fixed-back racing seats, ergonomic office chairs, and a comprehensive range of custom brackets engineered for specific vehicle models. Corbeau emphasizes a perfect-fit approach, pairing each seat with a bracket built for the exact make and model, eliminating the guesswork of mixing components from different suppliers.

The company serves motorsport enthusiasts, automotive aftermarket customers, gamers, and office professionals worldwide. Its seats are marketed for street driving, track competition, off-road use, gaming setups, and workplace ergonomics, with examples such as the Trailcat, FX1 Pro, RRS, and A4 models.

